## Case: pipe-neighbor-binop
id: "av.parity.1080.pipe-neighbor-binop"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1080", "calls"]
links: ["PLAN-1080"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.at"

```auto
type T {
    v int
    fn get() int { return .v }
}
fn main() int {
    let t = T(7)
    let a = t |> .get() - 1
    let b = 10 - (t |> .get())
    return a * 100 + b
}
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
exit: 603

### Probe a2r
recipe: "ac-a2r/hir-language-run-v1"
profile: "language"
entry: "main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1"]
exit: 0

#### stdout

```text
value:603
```

### Notes

PIPE-NEIGHBOR (frozen auditable normalization, §6.5 D-03): the pipe binds
its immediately-preceding suffix chain TIGHTLY — `t |> .get() - 1` =
`(t |> .get()) - 1` = 6, and a parenthesized pipe chain is a normal
operand (`10 - (t |> .get())` = 3; total 6*100+3 = 603). The legacy
engine's lower-binding `(x + y) |> .m()` shape is written with explicit
parentheses on the left operand here; the separated `| >` tokens and
`is`-arm patterns keep their own meanings
(pipe-neighbor-token-separation).

## Case: pipe-neighbor-token-separation
id: "av.parity.1080.pipe-neighbor-token-separation"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1080", "calls"]
links: ["PLAN-1080"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.at"

```auto
fn main() int {
    if 8 > (4 | 2) {
        return 3
    }
    return 0
}
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
exit: 3

### Probe a2r
recipe: "ac-a2r/hir-language-run-v1"
profile: "language"
entry: "main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1"]
exit: 0

#### stdout

```text
value:3
```

### Notes

PIPE-NEIGHBOR: `|` (bitwise) and `>` (comparison) keep their separate
meanings — `4 | 2` is 6, `8 > 6` is true, so the branch fires; the
two-character `|>` pipe token never swallows the separated pair. `is`-arm or-patterns live in
the statement pattern grammar (not the expression postfix surface) and
are untouched by the pipe step.

